diagnostics/constructor-and-enum-habits.em:5:9: `Point` has no type-level member named `new`
  var p = Point.new(1, 2)
          ^^^^^^^^^
A value is built by calling the type's name, with no `.new`: write `Point(1, 2)`.
diagnostics/constructor-and-enum-habits.em:9:16: `red` is not defined
  var c: Color = red
                 ^^^
`red` is a choice of `Color`, so write it with the type: `Color.red`.
